    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Fast and slow pointers</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Cycle detection</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/happy-number/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 202</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Happy Number</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Repeatedly replace n by the sum of the squares of its digits; is 1 ever reached? The sequence is a linked list whose \"next\" is a function, so it either hits the fixed point 1 or falls into a cycle. A hash set detects the repeat; Floyd's tortoise and hare does it in O(1) space.</p>\n"
  },
